  "title": "US blacklists Megaspeed as Huang returns; Black Friday brings few real GPU deals",
  "summary": "After Jensen Huang's return as Nvidia CEO, the US put Singapore's Megaspeed on its trade blacklist and keeps probing alleged AI-chip exports to China; analyst Ming-Chi Kuo warns of tighter GPU sales rules. On the PC side, Black Friday prices are barely moving: RTX 50 cards still sell far above MSRP in the US, while a few smaller cards, a Ryzen 7 9800X3D coupon and some DDR5 kits got real discounts. Nvidia also shipped a driver hotfix for excessive SSD writes.",
  "takeaways": [
    "Black Friday GPU prices are still about 1.5-2x MSRP in the US; only small discounts on RTX 5060 Ti 8GB and RX 9070 GRE so far.",
    "Ryzen 7 9800X3D at $399 (Amazon coupon) is the best CPU deal right now.",
    "32GB DDR5-6000 still costs about $440-480 even on sale; buy only if you must.",
    "Update the Nvidia driver to 621.40 if your SSD shows heavy writes."
  ],
